{
  "id": "backspace_string_compare",
  "title": "Backspace String Compare",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "category": "Algorithms",
  "tags": [
    "Two Pointers",
    "String",
    "Stack",
    "Simulation"
  ],
  "description": "<p>Given two strings <code>s</code> and <code>t</code>, return <code>true</code> <em>if they are equal when both are typed into empty text editors</em>. <code>'#'</code> means a backspace character.</p> <p>Note that after backspacing an empty text, the text will continue empty.</p> <p> </p> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> s = \"ab#c\", t = \"ad#c\"\n<strong>Output:</strong> true\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Both s and t become \"ac\".\n</pre> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> s = \"ab##\", t = \"c#d#\"\n<strong>Output:</strong> true\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Both s and t become \"\".\n</pre> <p><strong class=\"example\">Example 3:</strong></p> <pre><strong>Input:</strong> s = \"a#c\", t = \"b\"\n<strong>Output:</strong> false\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> s becomes \"c\" while t becomes \"b\".\n</pre> <p> </p> <p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p> <ul> <li><code><span>1 &lt;= s.length, t.length &lt;= 200</span></code></li> <li><span><code>s</code> and <code>t</code> only contain lowercase letters and <code>'#'</code> characters.</span></li> </ul> <p> </p> <p><strong>Follow up:</strong> Can you solve it in <code>O(n)</code> time and <code>O(1)</code> space?</p>",
